/// Updates a trigger's mutable settings, including its name, status, prompt template, output configuration, session configuration, and schedule. Supply only the fields you want to change; `kind` and `webhook.provider` cannot be changed, and updating `session_template` replaces the stored template. Re-enabling a trigger does not produce a catch-up run, and schedule changes recompute `next_run_at`.
///
/// Partial update: only the supplied fields change. `kind` and `webhook.provider` are immutable (409 on change). Mutable: `name` (409 on duplicate), `status` (active&lt;-&gt;paused), `prompt_template`, `output`, `session_template` (fresh), `bound_session_id` (reuse), `cron.cron_expr` / `cron.timezone` (recomputes next_run_at). Re-enabling never produces a catch-up run. PATCHing session_template is a full replacement, so every spec.secrets slot value the new manifest declares must be resupplied (secret values are never echoed back), or the request is a 400.
///
/// [triggerId] The trigger UUID.
/// [name] New team-unique trigger name. Same charset/length rules as create.
/// [status] Trigger lifecycle state. Soft-deleted triggers are never returned
///   (404).
/// [promptTemplate] Optional `string` value serialized in the `prompt_template`
///   wire field.
/// [output] Output-delivery configuration on create/update. Exactly one of
///   email / slack is required for the matching mode and forbidden otherwise;
///   destinations are stored encrypted and never returned.
/// [sessionTemplate] fresh triggers only. A session_template PATCH is a full
///   replacement of the stored template; you must resupply every spec.secrets
///   slot value the new manifest declares, or the request is a 400.
/// [boundSessionId] reuse triggers only. UUID of an existing session owned by
///   the team.
/// [cron] cron block on create.
Future<GetTriggerResponse> harnessUpdateTrigger(ClientConfig config,
    {required String triggerId,
    SdkOptional<String> name = const SdkOmitted(),
    SdkOptional<TriggerStatus> status = const SdkOmitted(),
    SdkOptional<String> promptTemplate = const SdkOmitted(),
    SdkOptional<TriggerOutputWrite> output = const SdkOmitted(),
    SdkOptional<String> sessionTemplate = const SdkOmitted(),
    SdkOptional<String> boundSessionId = const SdkOmitted(),
    SdkOptional<CreateCronConfig> cron = const SdkOmitted(),
    RequestOptions? requestOptions}) async {
  if (name is SdkPresent<String>) {
    validateLength('name', name.value, min: 1, max: 64);
